usage: lotto [-t n] [-b n] [-n n] [-?]Lotto plays any of those games where you choose several numbers, andtry to match a random drawing.But it's more than just another random number generator - this one workson the principle that, the more you believe, the better it works! It includesa nearly infinite number of testimonials from real, actual people who haveused Lotto to change their lives.Switches:	-?	This message.	-h	Ditto.	-t	Sets the top number of the range (default 49)	-b	Sets the bottom number of the range (default 1)	-n	Sets the number of numbers to pick (default 6, maximum 0)Let me know when you make your first million!